## Session Management [advisory, workflow hook available]

At every significant milestone (feature complete, bug fixed, refactor done):
1. Call `checkpoint(summary, decisions, problems, files_changed, what_next)`
2. If the checkpoint says the project context needs review, update it
3. Keep local CC working docs updated (`STATUS.md`, local `devlog/`, and related CC docs)
4. Then commit what your repo policy allows to be tracked

At the start of every new session:
1. Call `read_status()` to understand current project state
2. Call `read_devlog(last_n=3)` to review recent changes
3. Then proceed with the task
## Commit Ceremony

The Commit Ceremony is mandatory for every significant commit.
`documentation_mode` changes ownership only; it never disables the ceremony.

Always update code, `STATUS.md`, and local `devlog/`. When impacted, also update
project context, `BUGS.md`, roadmap, and affected development docs.

Whether governed CC working docs are committed or kept local depends on
`cc_artifact_mode`. `devlog/` stays local session memory. In the recommended
adopter mode (`local_only`), the other CC working docs are still updated at
each milestone but remain gitignored.
## CodeWarden (optional - L2+)

